1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,860
Umako, hear me out!

2
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:06,740
Don't come any closer, you hear me?

3
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,800
These soaps are really growing on me.

4
00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:09,920
They're so engrossing.

5
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:15,520
Now, run away with me and we can be together.

6
00:00:16,240 --> 00:00:18,920
It makes me happy to hear you say that, but I'm sorry.

7
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:21,260
I just can't. It's just not possible.

8
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:23,700
I don't give a damn about the Count and his power.

9
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:26,440
All that should matter is how we feel for each other.

10
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:29,000
I really want to hold Master's hand.

11
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,080
I can't hear my heart, but

12
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:34,880
どうしたけ言うの?

13
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:38,440
胸のベルが鳴る

14
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:48,100
始まりはあの時だった

15
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:53,780
君が目の前に突然

16
00:00:53,780 --> 00:01:00,160
現れたのは生まれる前から

17
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:03,820
決められてたんだね

18
00:01:03,820 --> 00:01:06,120
きっとそうだよ

19
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:09,860
願いや野望や

20
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:11,860
空想が

21
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:15,280
知らないレベルへ

22
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:17,480
ドアを探して

23
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:19,780
羽ばたく旅と

24
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:20,960
未来を

25
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:22,460
触れる

26
00:01:22,460 --> 00:01:27,020
I can't hear my heart, babe

27
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:29,860
止められないよ

28
00:01:29,860 --> 00:01:32,840
天使が鳴らしてる

29
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:35,540
大好きの合図だよね

30
00:01:35,540 --> 00:01:38,540
Can you hear my heart, babe

31
00:01:38,540 --> 00:01:41,120
どうしたって言うの?

32
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:43,620
聞いたことがない

33
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:46,540
胸のベルが鳴る

34
00:01:46,540 --> 00:01:49,620
これでもまだ

35
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:54,620
君は何も知らないけれど

36
00:01:54,620 --> 00:02:00,060
Culture

37
00:02:00,060 --> 00:02:01,580
The Age of Exploration

38
00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:04,380
heralded the start of a new age of cultural trade

39
00:02:04,380 --> 00:02:11,300
During this era, the Europeans became aware of countless other peoples and cultures

40
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:19,920
Of course, they viewed the inhabitants of the Americas as savages, but they were fascinated by the enormity of their culture and the wealth they possessed

41
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:25,600
If this sounds like a certain Angeloid who insists on referring to humans as bugs, you'd be correct

42
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:29,040
She may see us as insects, yet she is still drawn to us

43
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:30,020
Yes, I'm with you

44
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:31,780
You're referring to Nymph, aren't you?

45
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:34,400
Because that doesn't really sound like Icarus

46
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:35,340
Yes, Mikako

47
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:42,680
Fascinating, isn't it?

48
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:43,880
Hmm

49
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:45,800
That too, Pooch

50
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:47,800
You're in on this too

51
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:57,020
Hey, look, it's time for the cultural fair again

52
00:02:57,020 --> 00:02:58,520
Am I supposed to know what that is?

53
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:00,900
It's something we do at the private high school in town

54
00:03:00,900 --> 00:03:03,540
All the different classes and clubs set up booths

55
00:03:03,540 --> 00:03:06,340
They put on plays and concerts, you know, stuff like that

56
00:03:06,340 --> 00:03:14,860
Master, will you be taking part in the fair too?

57
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:16,840
No, it's a pain in my ass

58
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:19,260
Only way I would is if my class forced me to join

59
00:03:19,260 --> 00:03:22,360
The way I see it, I'm not in any club, so why should I even bother?

60
00:03:24,060 --> 00:03:25,620
I've been waiting for you, Tomoki

61
00:03:25,620 --> 00:03:28,260
We have a plan in the New World Discovery Club

62
00:03:28,260 --> 00:03:31,520
Look, we're currently recruiting skilled pilots

63
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:32,720
Screw you!

64
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:33,640
Don't say that

65
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:35,360
You should be honored to even be considered

66
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:37,100
Given how many members we have in the running

67
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:38,640
Now wait just a damn minute

68
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:40,680
When the hell did I ever join your club, huh?

69
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:43,040
Well, according to the student council registry

70
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:45,060
We have you down as a card-carrying member

71
00:03:45,060 --> 00:03:45,800
Conspiracy!

72
00:03:45,920 --> 00:03:47,340
Someone's out to get me, I swear!

73
00:03:48,140 --> 00:03:48,580
Wow!

74
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:50,640
These poor depraved children

75
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:53,420
What a pathetic excuse for an event

76
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:54,860
Look, Yoshitsune

77
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:56,800
They put a banner up for the cultural fair

78
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:58,380
I'm surprised they could afford that

79
00:03:58,380 --> 00:03:59,640
Let alone pay for the fair

80
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:02,120
Do they even know the meaning of the word, culture?

81
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:04,360
It's those face turds from the academy

82
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:07,740
They think highly of themselves

83
00:04:07,740 --> 00:04:10,560
They're from Sarami Academy, the private school I mentioned

84
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:13,480
The only reason we team up with them to put on this fair

85
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:16,300
Is because our school is so small being out here in the sticks

86
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:20,160
They don't seem very friendly

87
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:22,560
Time to watch the sparks fly

88
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:24,600
My goodness, Sukino

89
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:26,100
Are you seeing this?

90
00:04:26,580 --> 00:04:28,640
They're actually making flowers out of cardboard

91
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:29,980
It begs the question

92
00:04:29,980 --> 00:04:32,200
Can these cave people demonstrate culture

93
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:34,080
When they've barely discovered how to make fire?

94
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:34,860
Stupid yuppies!

95
00:04:34,940 --> 00:04:35,680
If you're so great

96
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:37,960
What the hell are you doing for the festival this year?

97
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:38,740
Let me guess

98
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:40,040
Something big and flashy

99
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:41,860
Well, we have something that works, yes

100
00:04:41,860 --> 00:04:44,840
We will be performing the classics

101
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:48,580
That's the dumbest idea I've ever heard

102
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:49,840
Did you hear that, Zoharo?

103
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:52,220
You're gonna put on some lame-ass boring playas

104
00:04:52,220 --> 00:04:53,820
If anybody would want to see that crap

105
00:04:53,820 --> 00:04:55,260
Why not just play a tape of Shakespeare

106
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:57,020
While you're at it, you freaking rich idiots?

107
00:04:57,600 --> 00:04:59,580
It wasn't referring to the theater

108
00:04:59,580 --> 00:05:01,820
You are such a moron, Tomo

109
00:05:01,820 --> 00:05:03,820
He was talking about doing classical music

110
00:05:03,820 --> 00:05:06,480
The poor cretin's never heard of classical music

111
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:08,360
It almost makes me feel bad for him

112
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:09,220
Come on, everyone

113
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:10,520
We'd better be on our way

114
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:13,520
I'm afraid this lack of civility may infect us

115
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:14,740
Way to go, genius

116
00:05:14,740 --> 00:05:15,800
That big mouth of yours

117
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:18,020
Just put an even bigger target on our backs

118
00:05:18,020 --> 00:05:18,940
Damn

119
00:05:18,940 --> 00:05:21,200
They just declared war, Zohara

120
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:23,080
Now we have to do something for the fair

121
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:23,900
Yeah, I saw that

122
00:05:23,900 --> 00:05:24,800
Any bright ideas?

123
00:05:24,880 --> 00:05:25,520
Well, we could

124
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:26,360
I got nothing

125
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:29,900
Attention, everyone

126
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:31,540
The Prez has arrived

127
00:05:31,540 --> 00:05:34,840
As your class president

128
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:36,920
I cannot allow this injustice

129
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:38,440
To stand another moment

130
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:41,300
If they're going to attack us with music

131
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:43,560
Then we shall retaliate with music

132
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:45,220
What do you say?

133
00:05:45,540 --> 00:05:46,700
Want to start a band?

134
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:47,700
A band?

135
00:05:47,860 --> 00:05:48,840
Like with instruments?

136
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:53,980
How the hell is she getting a tambourine

137
00:05:53,980 --> 00:05:55,380
To make a sound like that?

138
00:06:01,540 --> 00:06:03,580
This is hopeless

139
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:06,160
There's no way all of us talentless hacks

140
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:07,080
Will figure it out

141
00:06:07,080 --> 00:06:08,340
But

142
00:06:08,340 --> 00:06:10,160
What other choice do we have?

143
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:17,520
Master's hand

144
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:20,140
All I want to do is hold it

145
00:06:20,140 --> 00:06:20,980
But how?

146
00:06:22,060 --> 00:06:22,700
I know

147
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:25,520
I'll try really hard to play this tambourine

148
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:27,380
And when he tells me how good I did

149
00:06:27,380 --> 00:06:28,900
I'll grab it

150
00:06:28,900 --> 00:06:41,900
Nymph, that was awesome

151
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:42,620
Uh-huh

152
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:44,420
You know, you were really talented

153
00:06:44,420 --> 00:06:46,060
I had no idea

154
00:06:46,060 --> 00:06:48,120
You had an aptitude for music, Nymph

155
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:49,520
Well, I'm good with machines

156
00:06:49,520 --> 00:06:50,600
So maybe that's why

157
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:52,720
If we can somehow base the song

158
00:06:52,720 --> 00:06:53,960
Off of whatever you're playing

159
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:56,460
It won't sound so much like we're winging it

160
00:06:56,460 --> 00:06:57,760
Now we're cooking

161
00:06:57,760 --> 00:07:00,180
Let's show those private school douchebags

162
00:07:00,180 --> 00:07:01,000
A thing or two

163
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:03,320
I just want you to know

164
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:04,920
We'll all be depending on you, Nymph

165
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:06,640
To be perfectly honest

166
00:07:06,640 --> 00:07:08,420
I'm not that interested in being in a band

167
00:07:08,420 --> 00:07:09,920
But since I'm just killing time

168
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:11,200
I may as well help you out

169
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:12,860
Sweet, thank you

170
00:07:12,860 --> 00:07:19,820
The students from Sarami Academy

171
00:07:19,820 --> 00:07:21,500
Have decided to pick a fight with us

172
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:22,880
At the cultural fair this year

173
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:24,180
Therefore, by extension

174
00:07:24,180 --> 00:07:25,240
They have picked a fight

175
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:26,860
With the Satsukatane family

176
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:29,420
Of course, we live

177
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:31,680
This means war

178
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:34,160
And that is how Mikiko started

179
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:35,580
Her very own PR firm

180
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:38,280
With special thanks to the Satsukatane family

181
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:39,420
Almost immediately

182
00:07:39,420 --> 00:07:41,360
Sarami Hai's attendance to the fair

183
00:07:41,360 --> 00:07:42,640
Began to skyrocket

184
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:44,920
In direct opposition

185
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:46,880
The academy's PTA board

186
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:48,340
Called for an emergency rally

187
00:07:48,340 --> 00:07:49,940
To garner support for their side

188
00:07:49,940 --> 00:07:51,340
By pooling their money

189
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:53,240
They created their own PR machine

190
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:54,900
We will win this fight

191
00:07:54,900 --> 00:07:59,760
As both sides began to attack each other

192
00:07:59,760 --> 00:08:01,380
It drew the attention of the public

193
00:08:01,380 --> 00:08:02,960
Who then took to the streets

194
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:04,340
To protest for each cause

195
00:08:04,340 --> 00:08:05,020
Come with the academy

196
00:08:05,020 --> 00:08:07,700
We support you, Tamaki

197
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:13,520
The joint cultural fair's music contest

198
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:16,180
Split Sarami City into two warring factions

199
00:08:16,180 --> 00:08:18,420
Leaving it hanging on the edge of chaos

200
00:08:18,420 --> 00:08:19,860
Life was put on hold

201
00:08:19,860 --> 00:08:22,900
While everybody focused on their respective teams

202
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:24,080
Is it just me

203
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:26,440
Or is this whole thing getting completely out of hand?

204
00:08:26,540 --> 00:08:28,860
Yeah, I guess we better start practicing, huh?

205
00:08:28,860 --> 00:08:31,620
Icarus, do it again

206
00:08:31,620 --> 00:08:33,960
You're gonna have to do this live soon

207
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:35,740
You need more practice

208
00:08:35,740 --> 00:08:36,860
I'm sorry, Master

209
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:37,860
I'll work harder at it

210
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:46,240
Hey, Icarus

211
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:48,800
Yes, Soharma?

212
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:50,260
Something wrong?

213
00:08:50,460 --> 00:08:51,280
You seem blue

214
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:52,840
No matter what I try

215
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:54,920
I can't be of any help to Master

216
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:56,840
I wouldn't worry about that

217
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:57,460
Seriously

218
00:08:57,460 --> 00:08:58,660
I'm on drums

219
00:08:58,660 --> 00:09:00,080
And I barely know what I'm doing

220
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:01,780
I know, but

221
00:09:01,780 --> 00:09:03,000
That was perfect, Nymph

222
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,340
Absolutely perfect

223
00:09:04,340 --> 00:09:05,720
It wasn't even that hard

224
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:06,460
Okay, guys

225
00:09:06,460 --> 00:09:07,220
Let's go again

226
00:09:07,220 --> 00:09:07,900
From the top

227
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:11,420
Here's an idea, Icarus

228
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:12,480
Perhaps the tambourine

229
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:13,920
Isn't the best option for you

230
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:14,180
No

231
00:09:14,180 --> 00:09:15,860
Maybe there's something better

232
00:09:15,860 --> 00:09:16,880
You can do in the band

233
00:09:16,880 --> 00:09:17,880
Want to give it a try?

234
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:20,180
All right

235
00:09:20,180 --> 00:09:26,440
Whoa

236
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:27,400
How did

237
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:28,600
Whoa

238
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:39,400
Come on, come on

239
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:40,720
Now that the fair's here

240
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:41,740
I need to have some fun

241
00:09:41,740 --> 00:09:43,140
There's still a little time

242
00:09:43,140 --> 00:09:44,160
Before the performance

243
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:51,180
Welcome, Master

244
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:52,840
How many in your party today?

245
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:53,740
Icarus

246
00:09:53,740 --> 00:09:54,600
What the holy hell

247
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:55,480
Are you doing here?

248
00:09:55,820 --> 00:09:56,920
Someone in our class

249
00:09:56,920 --> 00:09:57,980
Said they needed my help

250
00:09:57,980 --> 00:09:58,880
So I'm helping

251
00:09:58,880 --> 00:09:59,500
Tomo

252
00:09:59,500 --> 00:10:00,580
What a nice surprise

253
00:10:00,580 --> 00:10:01,100
Welcome

254
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:01,860
Zahara

255
00:10:01,860 --> 00:10:02,760
Come on, buddy

256
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:04,200
Are you gonna order or what?

257
00:10:05,040 --> 00:10:05,780
I'll just

258
00:10:05,780 --> 00:10:07,000
Have a juice

259
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:07,780
And how about you?

260
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:08,920
Just a coffee

261
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:14,460
She's amazing

262
00:10:14,460 --> 00:10:15,780
Oh, gosh

263
00:10:15,780 --> 00:10:17,580
Tomo, can you stick around

264
00:10:17,580 --> 00:10:18,220
A little longer?

265
00:10:18,340 --> 00:10:19,600
Because I'm about to go on break

266
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:20,500
We should take a walk

267
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:21,000
Or something

268
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:21,700
Okay?

269
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:23,320
Um, yeah

270
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:23,980
Sure thing

271
00:10:23,980 --> 00:10:26,140
So, what are you having?

272
00:10:26,540 --> 00:10:27,660
A little more, please

273
00:10:27,660 --> 00:10:28,320
Huh?

274
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:30,260
Bend over a tad more

275
00:10:30,260 --> 00:10:37,540
I'm so excited for today

276
00:10:37,540 --> 00:10:39,020
Where do you guys think

277
00:10:39,020 --> 00:10:39,900
We should start?

278
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:45,240
Tomoki, check it out

279
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:45,640
What?

280
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:46,760
There's a haunted house

281
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:47,580
We should go

282
00:10:47,580 --> 00:10:50,500
Hey, wait

283
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:57,760
What are you up to?

284
00:10:58,540 --> 00:10:59,660
Just my exhibit

285
00:10:59,660 --> 00:11:01,880
I thought I'd take advantage

